  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Thursday 15 January 1903, for the places of Anthony Bunting, J. A. Thompson, William White (who had resigned some months before and was not replaced), Richard Soye and John Mahaffy. Eleven were nominated on Monday 5 January; J. A. Thompson and J. S. Carrick are not in the result. \"Of the 2,400 electors on the register 1,617 voted, of these over 500 polling within the last hour. There were only 16 spoiled voting papers.\" The News-Letter called it \"by far the heaviest\" poll in the history of Lurgan municipal elections; MacGeagh's 898 was the largest vote ever cast for a Lurgan candidate. Thomas Chambers was nominated by Joshua and James McNeice. No party labels printed."
